{{also|Appendix:Variations of "bed"}}
==English==

===Etymology===
[[File:Vrba postelja.jpg|thumb|right|A bed (furniture)]]

From {{inh|en|enm|bed}}, {{m|enm|bedde}}, from {{inh|en|ang|bedd}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*badi}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*badją|t=resting-place, plot of ground}}.
{{rel-top|cognates}}
Cognate with {{cog|frr|baad}}, {{m|frr|beed}}, {{cog|stq|Bääd}}, {{cog|fy|bêd}}, {{cog|nds|Bedd}}, {{cog|nl|bed}}, {{cog|de|Bett}}, {{cog|sv|bädd}}, {{cog|is|beður}}, all meaning “bed”.
{{rel-bottom}}
{{rel-top|further possible etymology and cognates}}
The {{inh|en|gem-pro|-}} term may in turn be from {{der|en|ine-pro|*bʰedʰh₂-|*bʰedʰ-|t=to dig}} with various theories explaining the development in meaning. If it is, the term is also cognate with {{cog|grc|βοθυρος||pit}}, {{cog|la|fossa||ditch}}, {{cog|lv|bedre||hole}}, {{cog|cy|bedd||grave}}, {{cog|br|bez||grave}}; and probably also {{cog|ru|бодать||to butt, gore}}.
{{rel-bottom}}

